## Global Shortcut Management

### Shortcut Registration Pattern
Global shortcuts in [src-tauri/src/lib.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/lib.rs):
```rust
use tauri::GlobalShortcutManager;

fn setup_global_shortcuts(app: &AppHandle) -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let app_handle = app.clone();

    // Spacebar for dictation
    app.global_shortcut_manager().register("Space", move |app, event| {
        handle_dictation_shortcut(app, event);
    })?;

    // Option+D for agent
    let app_handle = app.clone();
    app.global_shortcut_manager().register("Alt+D", move |app, event| {
        handle_agent_shortcut(app, event);
    })?;

    Ok(())
}

fn handle_agent_shortcut(app: &AppHandle, event: GlobalShortcutEvent) {
    let app_state = app.state::<AppState>();

    match app_state.get_agent_trigger_mode() {
        AgentTriggerMode::Tap => handle_tap_mode(app, event),
        AgentTriggerMode::Hold => handle_hold_mode(app, event),
    }
}
```

### Escape Key Dynamic Registration
Pattern for context-sensitive escape key:
```rust
pub fn register_escape_key(app: &AppHandle) -> Result<(), String> {
    app.global_shortcut_manager()
        .register("Escape", move |app, _| {
            // Handle escape based on current context
            if app.state::<AppState>().is_agent_active() {
                stop_agent_session(app);
            } else if app.state::<AppState>().is_dictation_active() {
                stop_dictation_session(app);
            }
        })
        .map_err(|e| e.to_string())
}

pub fn unregister_escape_key(app: &AppHandle) -> Result<(), String> {
    app.global_shortcut_manager()
        .unregister("Escape")
        .map_err(|e| e.to_string())
}
```

## Frontend-Backend Communication

### Event-Driven Updates
Frontend listens for backend events:
```typescript
// In App.tsx
useEffect(() => {
  const unlistenPromises = [
    listen('agent-transcription-start', handleAgentStart),
    listen('agent-committed', handleAgentCommit),
    listen('settings-changed', handleSettingsChange),
  ];

  return () => {
    unlistenPromises.forEach(async (unlisten) => {
      (await unlisten)();
    });
  };
}, []);
```

### Command Invocation Pattern
Frontend calls backend commands:
```typescript
import { invoke } from '@tauri-apps/api/tauri';

// Simple command
const mode = await invoke<AgentTriggerMode>('get_agent_trigger_mode');

// Command with parameters
await invoke('set_agent_trigger_mode', { mode: 'Hold' });

// Error handling
try {
  const result = await invoke<string>('risky_command', { param: value });
  // Handle success
} catch (error) {
  console.error('Command failed:', error);
  // Handle error
}
```

